{"version":3,"createdAt":1791623472399,"mainModel":{"schemaVersion":8,"id":"cm_mv26ag67","key":"cm_mv26ag67","name":"Planchard Chapter1 - review Q1-Q15 - browser 2026-10-10","kind":"part","authoringMode":"fully-parametric","localFrame":{"origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0},"xAxis":{"x":1,"y":0,"z":0},"yAxis":{"x":0,"y":1,"z":0},"zAxis":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":1}},"references":[{"id":"origin","type":"origin","name":"Origin","origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0}},{"id":"plane:top","type":"plane","name":"Top Plane","origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0},"normal":{"x":0,"y":1,"z":0},"xAxis":{"x":1,"y":0,"z":0}},{"id":"plane:front","type":"plane","name":"Front Plane","origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0},"normal":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":1},"xAxis":{"x":1,"y":0,"z":0}},{"id":"plane:right","type":"plane","name":"Right Plane","origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0},"normal":{"x":1,"y":0,"z":0},"xAxis":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":1}},{"id":"axis:x","type":"axis","name":"X Axis","origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0},"direction":{"x":1,"y":0,"z":0}},{"id":"axis:y","type":"axis","name":"Y Axis","origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0},"direction":{"x":0,"y":1,"z":0}},{"id":"axis:z","type":"axis","name":"Z Axis","origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0},"direction":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":1}}],"parameters":{},"sketches":[{"id":"sk_2oh9r","name":"X·Z sketch","plane":"top","offset":0,"referenceId":"plane:top","points":[],"entities":[],"constraints":[],"diagnostics":[],"status":"fully-defined"}],"features":[],"history":[],"parts":[],"assemblies":[],"appearances":[],"notes":[],"markups":[],"rules":{},"metadata":{"authoringSystem":"parametric-v1"},"topologyBindings":[],"namedSelections":[],"revision":1,"lastRebuild":{"ok":true,"signature":"{\"definitionId\":\"cm_mv26ag67\",\"features\":[],\"history\":[{\"id\":\"history:sketch:sk_2oh9r\",\"kind\":\"sketch\",\"suppressed\":false,\"targetId\":\"sk_2oh9r\"}],\"overrides\":{},\"revision\":1,\"sketches\":[{\"constraints\":[],\"entities\":[],\"id\":\"sk_2oh9r\",\"name\":\"X·Z sketch\",\"offset\":0,\"plane\":\"top\",\"points\":[],\"referenceId\":\"plane:top\"}]}","issues":[],"rebuiltAt":1791623464953},"price":500,"col":"#c9bfae","constraints":[],"rollback":null,"activeSketch":"sk_2oh9r","variables":[],"referenceGeometry":[],"definitionId":"cm_mv26ag67","documentVersion":1,"context":{"kind":"part","units":{"length":"mm","angle":"deg","mass":"kg","precision":3},"activeCoordinateSystemId":"origin"},"customProperties":{"Description":"Chapter1 reviewQuestions1-15 printed1-51/PDF79. Independent source-grounded explanations, not publisher answer key. Source2021 mechanical drafting conventions stated; actual Chrome note worksheet, no dummy CAD."},"drawing":{"version":1,"draftingStandard":"custom","secondaryUnits":"","secondaryPrecision":2,"size":"A3","orientation":"landscape","projection":"third","units":"mm","scale":"fit","showHidden":true,"showCenters":true,"showZones":true,"views":[],"dims":[],"notes":[{"id":"nfiqqhz6","x":34.755904449194375,"y":24.64126801587906,"text":"CHAPTER1 - REVIEW ANSWERS Q1-Q15\nSource: printed1-51 / PDF79, Planchard2021.\nIndependent explanations under the book mechanical-drafting convention.\nQuestions summarized; no official answer-key or physical-model claim.","leader":null},{"id":"n3dxtmtv","x":34.755904449194375,"y":59.6884669389522,"text":"Q1 - Cartesian coordinates\nPerpendicular X,Y,Z axes locate a point by signed distances from\na common origin. In a2D sketch use two axes; the third describes\nthe normal/depth direction.","leader":null},{"id":"nnp17hbg","x":34.755904449194375,"y":84.7221948616938,"text":"Q2 - Axis intersection\nThe origin, with coordinates(0,0,0), or(0,0)in2D.","leader":null},{"id":"nxcrnrce","x":34.755904449194375,"y":109.75590444919439,"text":"Q3 - Right-hand rule\nPoint the right-hand index along+X and middle finger along+Y; the\nthumb points+Z. Equivalently curl from+X toward+Y and the thumb\ngives+Z. Positive rotation curls around a positively directed\naxis with the thumb along that axis.","leader":null},{"id":"nv43dynn","x":34.755904449194375,"y":134.78961403669499,"text":"Q4 - Freehand sketching\nIt communicates and tests shape, proportions and spatial\nrelationships quickly, before detailed CAD or manufacturing\ndimensions.","leader":null},{"id":"nos4o761","x":34.755904449194375,"y":159.8233419594366,"text":"Q5 - First versus third angle\nFirst angle places the object between observer and projection\nplane; Top is below Front and Right is left of Front. Third angle\nplaces the plane between observer and object; Top is above Front\nand Right is right of Front.","leader":null},{"id":"nn64dnrm","x":34.755904449194375,"y":184.85705154693719,"text":"Q6 - US first-angle statement\nFalse under the book's US convention: the book uses third-angle\nprojection.","leader":null},{"id":"nec1lvfj","x":34.755904449194375,"y":209.89076113443778,"text":"Q7 - Line precedence\nWhen lines coincide, draw the higher-priority one:\nVisible,Hidden,Cutting-plane,Center,Phantom,Break,Dimension,Extension/Leader,Section.\nA visible edge replaces a coincident hidden line; a hidden line\noverrides a coincident centerline. Source priority list is\nPDF51/1-23.","leader":null},{"id":"nhu9ao13","x":34.755904449194375,"y":234.9244890571794,"text":"Q8 - Hidden overrides visible\nFalse. A visible/object line takes priority over a coincident\nhidden line.","leader":null},{"id":"npazzkvy","x":225.01213765172912,"y":59.6884669389522,"text":"Q9 - 2D quadrants\nTrue: two intersecting perpendicular axes divide the plane into\nquadrantsI–IV. Conventional numbering starts upper-right and\nproceeds counterclockwise.","leader":null},{"id":"ncg9fd6c","x":225.01213765172912,"y":84.7221948616938,"text":"Q10 - Glass box\nPlace the part inside a transparent box, project perpendicular to\neach face, then unfold the faces into the chosen\nfirst-/third-angle arrangement. The aligned views show\nwidth,height,depth consistently.","leader":null},{"id":"nh7ffk75","x":225.01213765172912,"y":109.75590444919439,"text":"Q11 - Same six views\nTrue. Front,Back,Top,Bottom,Left,Right view directions are the\nsame; the sheet arrangement changes.","leader":null},{"id":"neng3ef7","x":225.01213765172912,"y":134.78961403669499,"text":"Q12 - Hatch material indication\nTrue. Section hatch conventions can distinguish material types; a\nmaterial specification can still be needed for an exact grade.","leader":null},{"id":"nqgw1y70","x":225.01213765172912,"y":159.8233419594366,"text":"Q13 - Mechanical dimension endings\nTrue within the book's stated mechanical-drawing rule: dimension\nlines end with arrowheads. Architectural slash/dot practice is\nseparately identified in the source.","leader":null},{"id":"nizo9ktl","x":225.01213765172912,"y":184.85705154693719,"text":"Q14 - Break lines\nTrue with distinction: they mark an omitted portion/imaginary\nbreak. A long shaft can be shortened on paper; a broken-out view\nexposes a local interior. A full section uses a\ncutting-plane/section-view convention.","leader":null},{"id":"nirk7jnt","x":225.01213765172912,"y":209.89076113443778,"text":"Q15 - Front selection\nTrue as a design guideline. Choose the most informative\norientation with few hidden lines; project the other views from\nit. Its name need not match the part's installed front.","leader":null}],"primitives":[],"title":{"revision":"A","sheet":1,"sheets":1,"title":"CHAPTER1 - REVIEW Q1-Q15","number":"PLANCHARD 1-51 / PDF79","author":"","company":"","material":"","finish":"","mass":"","date":"2026-10-10","tolerance":""},"seeded":true},"lastStandardsAudit":{"at":1791623454965,"ok":true,"checked":0,"blocking":[]},"exactTopologyCache":{}},"assemblies":[],"drawings":[],"metadata":{"generator":"ModelForge CAD SolidWorks-Class","units":"mm","attachmentStorage":"content-addressed","activeDocument":{"type":"part","key":"cm_mv26ag67"}},"attachments":[]}